Description: analyzer for malicious Office documents with VBA/XLM emulation
 MaldocTrace extracts VBA and Excel 4.0 (XLM) macros from Office documents,
 deobfuscates them and emulates them in a fully simulated environment: no
 process is started, no network request is made and no COM object is
 created. The report shows what the document would do (command lines,
 decoded payloads, dropped files), each traced back to the module,
 procedure and line, or sheet and cell, that produced it.
 .
 Supported inputs are OLE/CFB (.doc, .xls, .ppt),
 OOXML (.docx, .docm, .xlsx, .xlsm, .pptm), RTF, Word 2003 XML, Flat OPC,
 MHT (ActiveMime) and plain VBA text, also
 inside ZIP and 7z archives (encrypted ones are tried with the usual
 sample passwords) and .eml/.msg emails, all analyzed in memory.
 It also reports macro-less techniques such as remote template injection,
 external OLE objects, DDE fields, RTF Equation Editor exploits and VBA
 stomping.
 .
 Output is available as text, JSON and JSONL, with a batch mode for
 directories and an option to dump recovered payloads.
